    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d841">

                <pb facs="0794" n="694" xml:id="pg694"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">311.6124/15a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Commissioner at
                        Helsingfors</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Haynes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-07T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Situation is developing in Latvia in such a way as to make it unlikely that
                    deported aliens can be transferred to Bolshevik Russia through Libau. Telegraph
                    urgently whether it would be possible to arrange for their transfer through
                    Hangö. They number 249. The ship would reach Hangö probably January 12. This
                    Government would, of course, bear all expense connected with the transfer.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
